    {
      "@id": "docs/research-and-analysis/prior-art.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "beans and Beads",
      "prov:value": "- **Question for the owner (`b91x` / `q2aj`):** given that `beans` is\n  dormant-but-stable on plain Markdown files while `Beads` (`v1.3.2`) is still\n  working through multi-clone Dolt sync, merge and migration edge cases, should\n  we **(a) keep `beans`** (and either close the watch or recheck again after\n  2026-12-23 as originally scheduled in `b91x`), **(b) trial `Beads` alongside\n  `beans`** in a single isolated workspace, **(c) fork/maintain `beans`** (or\n  lean on our in-tree TypeScript tooling), or **(d) plan a migration to\n  `Beads`**?",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-12-23",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-12-23"
      ]
    },
